# fix symmetry example: relaxation of an LJ FCC crystal with the full
# cubic symmetry of the FCC structure (space group Fm-3m)
#
# The symmetry file was written with the find-symmetry tool:
#   find-symmetry -g 225 -s 4 4 4 -o fm-3m.json
# It contains the 192 operators of the conventional cubic unit cell and
# a supercell entry for the 4 x 4 x 4 unit cells in the box.  With all
# translations between unit cells included, every atom is related to
# every other atom and there are no free coordinates: only the volume
# of the box can change.  The minimization with fix box/relax finds the
# lattice constant at zero pressure for this potential.

units           lj
atom_style      atomic

lattice         fcc 0.8442
Lattice spacing in x,y,z = 1.6795962 1.6795962 1.6795962
region          box block 0 4 0 4 0 4
create_box      1 box
Created orthogonal box = (0 0 0) to (6.7183848 6.7183848 6.7183848)
  1 by 2 by 2 MPI processor grid
create_atoms    1 box
Created 256 atoms
  using lattice units in orthogonal box = (0 0 0) to (6.7183848 6.7183848 6.7183848)
  create_atoms CPU = 0.000 seconds
mass            1 1.0

pair_style      lj/cut 2.5
pair_coeff      * * 1.0 1.0
pair_modify     shift yes

fix             sym all symmetry fm-3m.json
fix             relax all box/relax iso 0.0

variable        a equal lx/4
thermo_style    custom step pe press vol v_a
thermo_modify   format float %14.8g
print           "Initial lattice constant: $(lx/4:%.8f)"
Initial lattice constant: 1.67959619
min_modify      line quadratic
minimize        0.0 1.0e-10 1000 10000

